    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today's slate with **Junior Caminero** (75.43) and **Yordan Alvarez** (71.66) anchoring the heart of the order as our premier options. **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Bassitt, where his elite xwOBA of .374 and the +19% SP skill adjustment propel him to the top of our rankings despite a slight park penalty. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start against Kirby; his explosive 71.66 score is driven by an elite .464 xwOBA and a strategic +7% platoon advantage, proving that even against a competent arm, his floor remains safely in the elite tier. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** (64.19) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.44) serve as our primary engines for stolen bases; **Caleb Durbin** is a high-upside play against Chandler given the SP's slow delivery, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leverages his top-of-the-order spot to maximize his scoring potential against Liberatore.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Chase Meidroth**, whose 39.26 score narrowly missed the 40-point threshold required for a start. While he benefited from a park boost, the SP skill adjustment against Jobe proved too punitive to justify a start, forcing us to lean toward the slightly higher-floor production of **Colt Keith** (45.63). We remain cautious regarding the platoon matchups for **Colt Keith** and **Carson Benge** (42.01), both of whom are facing same-sided pitching, which limits their ceiling today. Furthermore, **Dillon Dingler** (56.52) is currently our most sensitive start; while his +14% dynamic platoon advantage against Newcomb is promising, he remains a marginal play that we will be monitoring closely as official lineups finalize. Owners should note that **Lars Nootbaar**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** are unavailable today due to off-days or benching, limiting our flexibility should any late-scratch risks arise among the active squad.",
